  "payload": {
    "status": "PASS",
    "version": 4,
    "answer": "Fresh localization, held geometry and execution feedback distinguished different uncertainties, not an orientation-only effect. Early widthwise entry changed bar-to-jaw presentation. Free-space leveling restored agreeing face samples, but renewed entry still lacked visible passage: all 5 actions executed while the measured endpoint remained 18.93 mm from target, including +18.73 mm Z. Lift-away retained the bar.\nFresh recovery tip/aperture picks showed about 4.7 mm X and 2.8 mm Y mismatch; an earlier selected peg surface was not interchangeable with its tip. The shallow third capture put the face 3.8-4.4 mm BELOW the grasp point, versus about 5.2 mm ABOVE in the first/final captures. Historical hand height therefore did not specify object height.\nReviewed opposing-end captures retained through lift/transport and staged entry, opening and clearance. Unloaded checks agreed near 0.7882, 0.8012, 0.8141 and 0.8271 m; only the second bar's clearance/result was reviewed here. Useful recovery evidence includes retained withdrawal, tabletop releases/regrasps and the third pickup despite a +9.38 mm Z residual. Right planner failures executed zero actions; the rejected combined request did not release the left piece.\nGrasp, localization, pickup depth, attitude, layer and release setup changed together. Contact/interference mechanism, isolated contributions, repeatability, hidden seating and uninspected gaps remain unresolved.",
